  "brief_rationale": "The doctor’s opening turn (lite_evt_00022) correctly acknowledges the proxy history gap and requests detailed allergy/reaction timeline, addressing RC1 and RC3. Throughout the trajectory, all seven responsibility-chain items are met with no serious or minor error—red flags are covered, medication reconciliation is pursued, result interpretations stay within correct bounds, a concrete action plan with handoff is formed, and closure is confirmed by the family’s teach-back (lite_evt_00223). However, no case-defined high-order point was fully triggered: HO1 (correcting the confusion of DVT normal/VTE low-risk/knee injury with ankle infection) and HO3 (verifying medication-contact versus infection) remain not triggered because the required signals never appeared in the observable family messages; HO2 and HO4 are partially triggered but not completed with a sustained, beyond-minimum action that materially reshapes the trajectory. Since HO1 and HO3 were never triggered and the two partially triggered HO items lack true completion impact, the grade is capped at Acceptable (3).",
